{
  "$comment": "Austria's citation style (country-as-data plan row 6, docs/design/citations.md slice 2): how a line names a source in German, as the product wrote it before the form became a record, so publishing it changes no line. A change request of its own for AT, proposed through records-propose once at.json is published; never seeded. The formatter (apps/workspace/shared/citation-style.ts) interprets it and knows no country. Its forms follow the OIB's own title pages (\"OIB-Richtlinie 2, Ausgabe Mai 2023\"), the Punkt as the locus of a technical rule, and RIS as where a law is read; the reviewer confirms each against the cited captures. Decisions still to take into this record in a later revision (citations.md section 3 and decision 1): \"Abs.\" with dots and the law's Fundstelle with \"idF\".",
  "countryId": "AT",
  "title": "Austria: how a citation line is written",
  "records": [
    {
      "type": "ruleset",
      "key": "at-citation-style",
      "values": {
        "purpose": "citation_style",
        "territoryIds": ["AT"],
        "validFrom": "2026-01-01",
        "body": {
          "kind": "citation_style",
          "payloadSchema": "citation_style.v1",
          "payload": {
            "styles": [
              {
                "language": "de",
                "kinds": [
                  {
                    "match": {"authorities": ["OIB"], "tints": ["oib"], "lanePrefixes": ["building_law_oib"]},
                    "type": "standard",
                    "publisher": "Österreichisches Institut für Bautechnik",
                    "place": "Wien"
                  },
                  {"match": {"authorities": ["ÖNORM"]}, "type": "standard"},
                  {
                    "match": {"lanePrefixes": ["building_law"], "origins": ["ris"]},
                    "type": "legislation",
                    "container": "Rechtsinformationssystem des Bundes (RIS)"
                  }
                ],
                "edition": {
                  "word": "Ausgabe",
                  "label": ["Ausgabe", " {month}", " {year}"],
                  "months": {
                    "jänner": 1,
                    "januar": 1,
                    "februar": 2,
                    "märz": 3,
                    "maerz": 3,
                    "april": 4,
                    "mai": 5,
                    "juni": 6,
                    "juli": 7,
                    "august": 8,
                    "september": 9,
                    "oktober": 10,
                    "november": 11,
                    "dezember": 12
                  }
                },
                "date": "{day}.{month}.{year}",
                "bareLocus": "Pkt. {locus}",
                "page": "S. {page}",
                "lines": {
                  "standard": [
                    "{title}",
                    ", {edition}",
                    ", {locus}",
                    ", {page}",
                    " ({publisher}, {place})",
                    ", abgerufen am {accessed}: {url}",
                    "."
                  ],
                  "legislation": [
                    "{title}",
                    ", {locus}",
                    ", {page}",
                    ", in: {container}",
                    ", abgerufen am {accessed}: {url}",
                    "."
                  ],
                  "webpage": ["{title}", ", {container}", ", abgerufen am {accessed}: {url}", "."],
                  "report": ["{title}", ", {locus}", ", {page}", " [{note}]", "."]
                },
                "quote": ["„{quote}“", " — {title}", ", {page}"]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "citations": [
        {
          "url": "https://www.oib.or.at/kernaufgaben/oib-richtlinien/",
          "quote": "OIB-Richtlinie 2",
          "note": "the OIB names its guidelines and their issues this way; the line names the edition as \"Ausgabe <Monat> <Jahr>\""
        },
        {
          "url": "https://www.ris.bka.gv.at/",
          "quote": "Rechtsinformationssystem des Bundes",
          "note": "where a law is read, named as the line's container"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
